meta {
  name: Update course
  type: http
  seq: 14
}

put {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/courses/:id
  body: json
  auth: none
}

params:path {
  id: 41
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "Saturday stick (long legs)"
  }
}

docs {
  Target is 41 "straight marks", a scratch user course (rename it back or
  delete it afterwards). A built-in (34-38) answers 403: they are read-only,
  copy-only.

  The PUT bumps `version`, which invalidates the compiled scripted route for
  the shape — that is why the course editor re-POSTs /courses/sim-route.
}

